<title>CHINA: ASEAN RESOURCES YEARLY NET RISES 43 PCT.</title>
<headline>ASEAN RESOURCES YEARLY NET RISES 43 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   23.82   vs 18.65</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    5.0     vs 3.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil     vs nil</p>
<p>    Net profit		   244.19  vs 170.36</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,239.6 vs 1,005.0</p>
<p>    Company name		 Asean Resources Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 16-23</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 23</p>
<p>NOTE - Asean Resources is a property investment and management company. It also manufactures leather goods.</p>
<p>The exceptional item for the year ended March 31, 1996, representing the gain on disposal of property interests, has been reclassified as non-exceptional operating profit as it is now apparent that the selling of property interests has become a regular activity of the group and will continue to be one of its major sources of income.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 6.5 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 1.5 cents) vs 4.5 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
